WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:01.700
On

00:00:01.700 --> 00:00:02.900
the hillsides of Nantou County

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:03.900
in central Taiwan , you can see

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:05.400
the same kind of tree everywhere

00:00:05.466 --> 00:00:06.333
, straight and slender,

00:00:06.333 --> 00:00:07.833
topped with a canopy that looks

00:00:07.833 --> 00:00:08.800
like coconut leaves

00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:09.900
. This is betel nut.

00:00:10.100 --> 00:00:12.100
Taiwanese people call it "Taiwanese chewing gum."

00:00:12.133 --> 00:00:13.400
But the economic scale behind it

00:00:13.466 --> 00:00:16.066
far exceeds that

00:00:16.066 --> 00:00:18.300
of any chewing gum.

00:00:18.533 --> 00:00:19.766
At its peak in 1996,

00:00:19.766 --> 00:00:21.366
the planting area of ​​betel nut in Taiwan

00:00:21.366 --> 00:00:23.700
reached an astonishing 56,600 hectares.

00:00:23.800 --> 00:00:24.800
To put this into perspective,

00:00:25.066 --> 00:00:27.600
the total area of ​​Taipei City is 27,000 hectares.

00:00:27.866 --> 00:00:29.533
The planting area of ​​betel nut is

00:00:29.533 --> 00:00:31.733
more than twice the area of ​​Taipei City.

00:00:31.966 --> 00:00:34.600
From planting, harvesting, processing to sales,

00:00:34.700 --> 00:00:35.666
the entire industrial chain

00:00:35.666 --> 00:00:36.933
supports millions of people

00:00:36.933 --> 00:00:38.566
and 400,000 betel nut stalls. So

00:00:38.700 --> 00:00:39.866
what kind of business is

00:00:39.866 --> 00:00:40.566
this fruit

00:00:40.566 --> 00:00:42.400
in Taiwan ?

00:00:42.700 --> 00:00:44.866
How did it evolve from an indigenous social etiquette

00:00:44.866 --> 00:00:46.766
into a livelihood for Taiwanese farmers?

00:00:46.933 --> 00:00:48.700
With the explosion of Taiwan's economic miracle

00:00:48.700 --> 00:00:50.200
, it also gave rise to the

00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:52.366
unique betel nut beauty culture.

00:00:52.466 --> 00:00:53.700
Hello everyone, I'm Fat Cat

00:00:53.733 --> 00:00:56.133
. We've talked about convenience stores and bubble tea before.

00:00:56.300 --> 00:00:58.966
Today, let's talk about another Taiwanese industry phenomenon:

00:00:59.166 --> 00:00:59.966
the betel nut industry.

00:01:02.066 --> 00:01:03.133
At the beginning of the program,

00:01:03.133 --> 00:01:04.700
I'd like to ask you a question:

00:01:04.766 --> 00:01:06.966
How long have Taiwanese people been chewing betel nut? If we

00:01:06.966 --> 00:01:08.633
start counting from the earliest written records

00:01:08.633 --> 00:01:10.166
of the Han Chinese,

00:01:10.266 --> 00:01:12.566
the earliest historical record we can find

00:01:12.566 --> 00:01:14.133
comes from the Kangxi era of the Qing Dynasty, in

00:01:14.333 --> 00:01:16.900
1696. The first prefect of Taiwan, Jiang Yuying

00:01:16.900 --> 00:01:18.600
, oversaw the compilation of the "Taiwan Prefecture Gazetteer."

00:01:18.766 --> 00:01:19.800
In the section on local products,

00:01:19.800 --> 00:01:21.100
he described the state of betel nut chewing

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:22.700
among Taiwanese people at that time as follows: "

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:23.600
Men who chew betel nut

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:24.533
..." Women, whether

00:01:24.566 --> 00:01:25.933
walking or

00:01:25.966 --> 00:01:26.966
lying down, always chew

00:01:27.166 --> 00:01:28.266
betel nut. Over time , their

00:01:28.333 --> 00:01:29.500
lips and teeth turn black.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.133
Even when they are so poor they can't afford food

00:01:31.266 --> 00:01:32.600
, betel nut is indispensable . This means that

00:01:32.600 --> 00:01:33.466
regardless of gender,

00:01:33.466 --> 00:01:34.933
they chew betel nut while walking or lying down.

00:01:35.133 --> 00:01:37.700
Even when their lips and teeth turn black, and their families are so poor they can't afford food

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:39.566
, they still can't do without it

00:01:39.566 --> 00:01:41.133
. If you trace this history

00:01:41.333 --> 00:01:44.533
back to the Taiwanese aboriginal people,

00:01:44.533 --> 00:01:45.966
it goes back even further

00:01:45.966 --> 00:01:48.100
. Archaeologists have discovered

00:01:48.100 --> 00:01:50.400
traces of betel nut chewing

00:01:50.466 --> 00:01:51.566
on the teeth of Taiwanese ancestors

00:01:51.566 --> 00:01:52.966
thousands of years ago

00:01:52.966 --> 00:01:55.066
in sites in Beinan, Pingding, and Kenting, Taitung.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.666
Whether it's the Amis in the east,

00:01:56.666 --> 00:01:57.800
the Paiwan in the south

00:01:57.800 --> 00:02:01.100
, or the widely distributed Pingpu people, many ethnic groups

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:01.933
have long

00:02:01.933 --> 00:02:03.366
regarded betel nut as

00:02:03.366 --> 00:02:05.166
an important social item,

00:02:05.333 --> 00:02:06.666
especially during ancestral worship and memorial

00:02:06.733 --> 00:02:08.066
ceremonies. Whether it's a sign of estrangement

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:10.000
or a distinguished guest arriving

00:02:10.066 --> 00:02:10.966
to celebrate a marriage,

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:11.733
locals

00:02:11.733 --> 00:02:13.066
will always offer betel nuts

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.700
as a way to express their most sincere feelings.

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:17.700
So when did

00:02:17.800 --> 00:02:18.966
betel nuts

00:02:18.966 --> 00:02:20.566
become a business?

00:02:20.566 --> 00:02:22.533
This dates back to the late Ming and early Qing dynasties when

00:02:22.533 --> 00:02:24.766
a large number of Fujianese immigrants came to Taiwan.

00:02:24.866 --> 00:02:26.566
Seeing

00:02:26.566 --> 00:02:28.333
the betel nut trees planted around the houses

00:02:28.600 --> 00:02:30.366
of the indigenous people, these immigrants followed suit,

00:02:30.500 --> 00:02:33.066
transforming the small amounts of betel nuts scattered in their courtyards

00:02:33.133 --> 00:02:35.766
into a "harvestable and transportable" crop.

00:02:35.766 --> 00:02:37.966
They then transported these trees back to Fujian to sell.

00:02:38.066 --> 00:02:39.533
Even during the Qing dynasty,

00:02:39.533 --> 00:02:41.133
betel nuts could be used to offset taxes.

00:02:41.333 --> 00:02:42.933
This shift in thinking

00:02:42.933 --> 00:02:45.366
was the first seed of the betel nut industry's industrialization.

00:02:45.366 --> 00:02:47.100
In 1895, the Japanese arrived in

00:02:47.266 --> 00:02:49.266
Taiwan, and the Governor-General's Office clearly stated its intention

00:02:49.266 --> 00:02:51.400
to fully develop the industry. Suppressing and banning betel nut:

00:02:51.566 --> 00:02:52.900
Japanese colonizers considered

00:02:53.066 --> 00:02:55.366
chewing betel nut, like foot binding and queues,

00:02:55.366 --> 00:02:57.800
to be a Taiwanese vice that needed to be reformed.

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.066
They viewed it as unsightly

00:02:59.066 --> 00:02:59.933
, unhygienic,

00:02:59.933 --> 00:03:00.800
and uncivilized. Under

00:03:00.800 --> 00:03:04.266
the colonial policy of "Industrial Japan, Agricultural Taiwan,"

00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:05.800
the Japanese preferred to promote

00:03:05.800 --> 00:03:07.366
the cultivation of strategic economic crops

00:03:07.366 --> 00:03:08.800
such as sugarcane and rice

00:03:08.966 --> 00:03:11.400
. Betel nut was extremely discouraged

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.900
in the agricultural policy during the colonial period.

00:03:13.300 --> 00:03:15.466
But have you ever considered this question:

00:03:15.566 --> 00:03:16.833
how high would the rebound be

00:03:16.833 --> 00:03:19.333
if a consumer demand that has existed since ancient times

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:21.166
but has been suppressed for 50 years were to

00:03:21.166 --> 00:03:23.066
be unleashed

00:03:23.066 --> 00:03:24.800
and stimulated by a huge economy?

00:03:24.800 --> 00:03:26.566
The answer will soon be revealed.

00:03:27.400 --> 00:03:29.933
In 1945, the Nationalist government took over Taiwan,

00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:31.466
and 47 years later, the February 28 Incident occurred.

00:03:31.466 --> 00:03:32.700
In 1949,

00:03:32.700 --> 00:03:34.600
the Kuomintang was overwhelmed with

00:03:34.600 --> 00:03:36.933
the massive evacuation . Their primary focus was on

00:03:36.933 --> 00:03:39.266
food security and the redistribution of farmland.

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:40.300
As for betel nut,

00:03:40.300 --> 00:03:41.733
the Nationalist government lacked

00:03:41.733 --> 00:03:44.200
the same drive for "civilizational reform" as the Japanese,

00:03:44.266 --> 00:03:45.533
adopting a "we don't have time

00:03:45.533 --> 00:03:47.400
, do whatever you want"

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:48.466
policy.

00:03:48.566 --> 00:03:50.300
Moreover, at that time, betel nut chewing

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:52.200
was mainly practiced by elderly people from Taiwan.

00:03:52.200 --> 00:03:55.366
Many of the 1.2 million mainlanders who emigrated to Taiwan with the Nationalist government

00:03:55.466 --> 00:03:57.133
didn't even know

00:03:57.333 --> 00:03:58.066
what betel nut was. It wasn't

00:03:58.066 --> 00:03:59.600
until the late 1950s

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:00.666
and early 1960s

00:04:00.766 --> 00:04:03.166
that betel nut cultivation began to gradually recover,

00:04:03.200 --> 00:04:04.733
and demand slowly increased.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:06.000
More importantly, at

00:04:06.200 --> 00:04:07.733
this time, Taiwan's economy

00:04:07.733 --> 00:04:09.366
was entering a period of rapid growth. During the period of rapid development,

00:04:09.466 --> 00:04:11.000
the manufacturing industry expanded rapidly,

00:04:11.000 --> 00:04:13.166
and export trade was booming. Factories

00:04:13.200 --> 00:04:14.666
, construction sites, and

00:04:14.666 --> 00:04:16.566
truck drivers filled the roads.

00:04:16.566 --> 00:04:18.433
A large number of blue-collar workers

00:04:18.433 --> 00:04:21.266
, relying on manual labor, emerged during this era. What were

00:04:21.366 --> 00:04:23.233
their daily working conditions

00:04:23.233 --> 00:04:24.266
like?

00:04:24.500 --> 00:04:26.500
Construction workers poured concrete under the scorching sun

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:28.366
, standing for eight or nine hours at a stretch.

00:04:28.500 --> 00:04:30.166
Long-haul truck drivers

00:04:30.166 --> 00:04:31.700
drove hundreds of kilometers from Taipei to Kaohsiung

00:04:31.766 --> 00:04:33.200
without stopping

00:04:33.400 --> 00:04:35.233
. Factory assembly line

00:04:35.233 --> 00:04:36.500
workers worked shifts

00:04:36.500 --> 00:04:38.666
, relying on willpower to get through the late nights.

00:04:38.900 --> 00:04:41.100
What these people needed most was a stimulant

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:43.133
, and areca nut was the best "antidote."

00:04:43.266 --> 00:04:44.866
Arecoline is an alkaloid with a

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:47.000
structure... Similar to nicotine

00:04:47.300 --> 00:04:48.600
, after entering the body, it

00:04:48.600 --> 00:04:49.866
stimulates the sympathetic nervous system

00:04:49.866 --> 00:04:51.266
, causing adrenaline secretion,

00:04:51.266 --> 00:04:52.266
increased heart rate, and

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:53.300
elevated blood pressure

00:04:53.300 --> 00:04:56.000
. The feeling is a brief period of alertness and excitement.

00:04:56.133 --> 00:04:57.566
This effect

00:04:57.566 --> 00:04:59.000
appears within 5 minutes

00:04:59.000 --> 00:05:01.166
of chewing and can last for 2 to 3 hours.

00:05:01.266 --> 00:05:02.900
For a driver who has to drive continuously

00:05:02.900 --> 00:05:04.366
for 8 hours,

00:05:04.366 --> 00:05:05.566
this is sufficient. Moreover,

00:05:05.700 --> 00:05:06.866
betel nut is cheap.

00:05:06.900 --> 00:05:08.500
In its heyday,

00:05:08.500 --> 00:05:09.633
a pack of betel nut cost

00:05:09.633 --> 00:05:11.400
less than a pack of cigarettes. Its

00:05:11.400 --> 00:05:12.700
fast onset and low price

00:05:12.766 --> 00:05:14.466
combined

00:05:14.466 --> 00:05:17.033
made the spread of betel nut among blue-collar workers

00:05:17.033 --> 00:05:18.533
incredibly fast.

00:05:18.866 --> 00:05:21.133
Drivers, construction workers, dockworkers

00:05:21.133 --> 00:05:22.666
, and factory workers were all chewing

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:25.266
it. Betel nut became a status symbol.

00:05:25.333 --> 00:05:26.166
On construction sites,

00:05:26.166 --> 00:05:28.666
you'd offer a betel nut to a stranger,

00:05:28.666 --> 00:05:30.500
and they'd accept it—everyone was on the same page.

00:05:30.566 --> 00:05:31.900
People who didn't have this habit

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:32.533
sometimes

00:05:32.533 --> 00:05:34.700
felt, "They're not like us."

00:05:34.866 --> 00:05:36.466
It's the same principle as offering

00:05:36.533 --> 00:05:38.366
a cigarette; among men, smoking and drinking go hand in hand—

00:05:38.366 --> 00:05:40.333
a gesture and a glance are enough.

00:05:40.333 --> 00:05:41.366
This social attribute

00:05:41.366 --> 00:05:43.600
meant that betel nut's penetration in blue-collar circles

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:45.166
didn't need advertising.

00:05:45.366 --> 00:05:46.366
On the other hand,

00:05:46.466 --> 00:05:47.600
betel nut was practically

00:05:47.600 --> 00:05:49.200
a savior for Taiwan's traditional agriculture

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.600
during its crisis.

00:05:50.700 --> 00:05:51.500
For example,

00:05:51.500 --> 00:05:53.733
before 1970, the hilly area in eastern Zhongpu Township, Chiayi County,

00:05:53.766 --> 00:05:56.166
the core betel nut producing region in Taiwan

00:05:56.166 --> 00:05:57.700
... The main crops planted were

00:05:57.700 --> 00:05:59.866
traditional drought-resistant crops such as

00:05:59.866 --> 00:06:01.666
longan, cassava, and bamboo shoots

00:06:01.666 --> 00:06:04.366
. After 1970, the government said that fruit tree agriculture

00:06:04.566 --> 00:06:05.100
and cash crops

00:06:05.100 --> 00:06:06.066
were more profitable

00:06:06.066 --> 00:06:08.700
, so the local area shifted to

00:06:08.700 --> 00:06:11.400
planting mainly citrus fruits such as oranges and grapefruits.

00:06:11.600 --> 00:06:13.000
In fact, this was a misguided approach.

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.300
The area was not suitable for

00:06:14.566 --> 00:06:15.766
Huanglongbing (HLB)

00:06:15.866 --> 00:06:17.466
in the mid-to-late 1970s,

00:06:17.466 --> 00:06:19.533
which caused heavy losses to fruit farmers in China and Portugal.

00:06:19.533 --> 00:06:21.166
Only then were the fruit trees cut down and

00:06:21.166 --> 00:06:22.466
replaced with areca nuts, which are resilient and resistant

00:06:22.466 --> 00:06:24.000
to HLB.

00:06:24.333 --> 00:06:26.366
The situation in the Pingdong Plain was similar.

00:06:26.366 --> 00:06:27.333
First, rice was planted

00:06:27.333 --> 00:06:28.200
, then wax apples, and

00:06:28.200 --> 00:06:29.566
finally areca nuts were planted.

00:06:29.700 --> 00:06:31.900
Moreover , areca nuts are very easy to grow and

00:06:31.900 --> 00:06:33.000
require little care. With its

00:06:33.100 --> 00:06:35.366
long lifespan, a single planting can yield harvests for many years, making it

00:06:35.466 --> 00:06:37.600
particularly suitable for elderly farmers with limited physical strength.

00:06:37.700 --> 00:06:39.366
The price is also more stable than rice.

00:06:39.600 --> 00:06:41.133
Therefore, with both supply and demand

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:42.200
booming and all parties benefiting

00:06:42.200 --> 00:06:44.500
, and farmers not needing to expend much effort,

00:06:44.566 --> 00:06:46.766
Taiwan's betel nut industry skyrocketed.

00:06:47.000 --> 00:06:48.133
The term "green gold"

00:06:48.133 --> 00:06:49.466
originated from this period.

00:06:49.466 --> 00:06:53.000
In 1986, Taiwan's betel nut planting area was 11,000 hectares,

00:06:53.333 --> 00:06:56.466
which surged to 33,400 hectares in 1989,

00:06:56.566 --> 00:06:58.566
nearly tripling in three years.

00:06:58.666 --> 00:07:01.533
The annual output value reached NT$7.3 billion,

00:07:01.666 --> 00:07:03.100
making it the third largest agricultural product after rice and

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:05.000
sugarcane.

00:07:05.100 --> 00:07:05.933
This speed

00:07:05.933 --> 00:07:07.433
was unprecedented

00:07:07.433 --> 00:07:08.733
in Taiwan's agricultural history.

00:07:08.900 --> 00:07:10.066
By 1990,

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:12.766
Taiwan had formed three major betel nut production bases:

00:07:12.900 --> 00:07:14.333
Pingtung, Nantou, and Chiayi.

00:07:14.366 --> 00:07:16.133
The harvest times of these three production areas

00:07:16.133 --> 00:07:16.933
overlapped and

00:07:16.933 --> 00:07:17.766
complemented each other, ensuring

00:07:17.766 --> 00:07:19.000
continuous supply throughout the year.

00:07:19.000 --> 00:07:20.366
From the consumer

00:07:20.366 --> 00:07:21.966
end to the farmers in the production areas

00:07:21.966 --> 00:07:24.400
, and then to the processing associations and wholesalers in the midstream,

00:07:24.400 --> 00:07:26.766
a complete industrial chain was basically formed,

00:07:26.766 --> 00:07:27.966
only lacking the last piece

00:07:28.166 --> 00:07:29.300
—that is, another

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:30.733
story we need to tell separately:

00:07:30.933 --> 00:07:32.400
the betel nut stand and the betel nut beauty.

00:07:32.500 --> 00:07:34.100
A retail format that you can't find anywhere else

00:07:34.100 --> 00:07:36.800
in the world except Taiwan.

00:07:39.066 --> 00:07:40.966
In 1976,

00:07:40.966 --> 00:07:42.466
in a place called Shuangdong in Nantou, Taiwan

00:07:42.800 --> 00:07:43.733
, Xie's mother

00:07:43.733 --> 00:07:46.066
sold betel nuts on the Shuangdong section of Zhongtan Highway

00:07:46.366 --> 00:07:48.166
. The highway is a major

00:07:48.166 --> 00:07:49.966
transportation route connecting Taichung to Puli and Sun Moon Lake,

00:07:50.000 --> 00:07:51.366
with heavy traffic.

00:07:51.366 --> 00:07:52.900
However, the family's betel nut stand

00:07:52.900 --> 00:07:53.766
wasn't doing very well;

00:07:53.766 --> 00:07:55.366
few people stopped to buy.

00:07:55.366 --> 00:07:57.266
One day, Mrs. Xie had a brilliant idea:

00:07:57.266 --> 00:07:59.100
she asked her three daughters,

00:07:59.133 --> 00:08:00.600
Xiuzhu, Xiuhua, and Xiulan,

00:08:00.600 --> 00:08:02.766
who worked in a factory, to help sell betel nuts at the stand

00:08:02.766 --> 00:08:04.966
. The three sisters were all under 20 years old at the time

00:08:04.966 --> 00:08:05.666
, beautiful

00:08:05.666 --> 00:08:07.066
, and had sweet smiles.

00:08:07.066 --> 00:08:09.200
As a result, the business was surprisingly good.

00:08:09.366 --> 00:08:10.766
After seeing this, people in the neighborhood

00:08:10.766 --> 00:08:11.466
followed suit

00:08:11.466 --> 00:08:13.066
and began to find their own daughters

00:08:13.066 --> 00:08:15.400
or hire young women to sell betel

00:08:15.700 --> 00:08:17.600
nuts. The three Xie sisters, known as

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:19.566
the "Betel Nut Beauties," are the pioneers of this tradition.

00:08:19.700 --> 00:08:21.333
Why are they called "Betel Nut Beauties"?

00:08:21.333 --> 00:08:22.933
This is thanks to Ye Qi. In 1985, Tian

00:08:22.933 --> 00:08:26.066
released the song "Betel Nut Girl,"

00:08:26.066 --> 00:08:28.100
which included the lyric, "

00:08:28.100 --> 00:08:29.966
Charming and lovely, like Xi Shi

00:08:30.000 --> 00:08:31.666
, everyone who sees her is captivated.

00:08:31.800 --> 00:08:33.866
" After the song became widely popular, the

00:08:33.866 --> 00:08:35.300
title "Betel Nut Beauty"

00:08:35.300 --> 00:08:36.333
stuck.

00:08:36.466 --> 00:08:37.466
However, back then,

00:08:37.566 --> 00:08:39.866
the attire of a "betel nut beauty" was relatively conservative;

00:08:39.866 --> 00:08:41.200
a short skirt and sleeveless top

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:42.766
were considered quite outrageous.

00:08:42.766 --> 00:08:45.366
The real change occurred in the 1990s

00:08:45.400 --> 00:08:47.566
with the rapid expansion of Taiwan's highway network.

00:08:47.566 --> 00:08:49.866
The areas around interchanges, frequented by truck drivers

00:08:49.866 --> 00:08:53.266
and freight convoys, became the most densely populated areas for betel nut stands,

00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:54.333
leading to fierce competition.

00:08:54.333 --> 00:08:55.700
Sometimes,

00:08:55.700 --> 00:08:57.800
more than a dozen betel nut stands lined up along

00:08:57.800 --> 00:08:59.666
a single road, all displaying the same green...

00:08:59.866 --> 00:09:02.266
How to get drivers to stop in front of you using

00:09:02.266 --> 00:09:03.600
betel nut leaves and white lime

00:09:03.866 --> 00:09:05.300
became an art . At its peak, betel nut beauties

00:09:05.300 --> 00:09:07.800
sat in brightly colored glass houses,

00:09:07.800 --> 00:09:09.133
with peacock lanterns and

00:09:09.133 --> 00:09:10.300
flashing neon lights hanging in front

00:09:10.366 --> 00:09:12.300
. They wore what might be sheer swimsuits

00:09:12.300 --> 00:09:13.733
or custom-

00:09:13.733 --> 00:09:16.066
designed uniforms.

00:09:16.100 --> 00:09:17.366
Drivers

00:09:17.366 --> 00:09:19.266
could see them through their car windows.

00:09:19.500 --> 00:09:22.400
The betel nut culture spread from provincial highways to highways throughout Taiwan;

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.466
wherever there was traffic, there were betel nut stands

00:09:24.566 --> 00:09:26.200
. Later, even overseas tourists

00:09:26.200 --> 00:09:27.300
came to see the betel nut

00:09:27.366 --> 00:09:28.533
beauties ,

00:09:28.533 --> 00:09:29.733
even if they didn't eat betel nuts

00:09:29.733 --> 00:09:30.733
. But at the same time,

00:09:30.866 --> 00:09:32.133
controversy accumulated

00:09:32.333 --> 00:09:33.866
regarding the betel nut beauties. The issue

00:09:33.866 --> 00:09:35.533
of betel nut beauties has been a subject

00:09:35.533 --> 00:09:36.733
of intense debate in Taiwanese society

00:09:36.766 --> 00:09:37.966
for many years, involving multiple levels and

00:09:37.966 --> 00:09:39.500
differing viewpoints from all sides.

00:09:39.500 --> 00:09:41.966
The first controversy is the objectification of women,

00:09:41.966 --> 00:09:43.300
which has been the longest-debated and most

00:09:43.300 --> 00:09:44.533
difficult to resolve.

00:09:44.700 --> 00:09:45.666
Opponents argue

00:09:45.666 --> 00:09:47.200
that the revealing clothing of betel nut beauties

00:09:47.333 --> 00:09:49.000
essentially uses women's bodies

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:50.600
as a tool for product promotion,

00:09:50.600 --> 00:09:52.066
constituting blatant objectification.

00:09:52.333 --> 00:09:53.366
Supporters

00:09:53.366 --> 00:09:54.366
counter

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.566
that it

00:09:56.566 --> 00:09:57.466
doesn't

00:09:57.466 --> 00:09:59.900
matter,

00:09:59.900 --> 00:10:01.133
models and entertainers also dress provocatively,

00:10:01.366 --> 00:10:02.900
yet legislation specifically regulates what betel nut beauties wear,

00:10:02.900 --> 00:10:04.933
which they consider class discrimination.

00:10:04.933 --> 00:10:06.866
The second issue is safety.

00:10:06.866 --> 00:10:08.133
The daring attire of betel nut

00:10:08.166 --> 00:10:10.500
beauties

00:10:10.500 --> 00:10:13.200
leads to driver distraction and frequent

00:10:13.333 --> 00:10:15.033
traffic accidents, which was

00:10:15.033 --> 00:10:18.000
the direct trigger for Taipei City's pioneering legislation to regulate their clothing

00:10:18.000 --> 00:10:19.500
in 2002. The third issue is that Taiwanese media

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:21.600
have long used betel nut beauties as a pornographic gimmick

00:10:21.600 --> 00:10:24.600
, amplifying visual stimulation while ignoring the family hardships , educational gaps, and structural poverty behind these girls.

00:10:24.700 --> 00:10:25.866
Few people ask

00:10:25.866 --> 00:10:27.333
why they are standing there.

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:30.366
In short, the betel nut beauty culture

00:10:30.366 --> 00:10:31.933
, a sales model that flourished

00:10:31.933 --> 00:10:32.666
for decades,

00:10:32.666 --> 00:10:34.533
is gradually fading away.

00:10:34.533 --> 00:10:35.866
However, Taiwanese society

00:10:35.866 --> 00:10:37.366
has to pay a huge social price

00:10:37.366 --> 00:10:39.400
for this prosperity

00:10:40.900 --> 00:10:42.466
.

00:10:42.466 --> 00:10:44.000
Most people dislike

00:10:44.100 --> 00:10:46.866
dizziness, chest tightness, throat constriction, rapid heartbeat, and

00:10:46.866 --> 00:10:47.566
general discomfort

00:10:47.566 --> 00:10:48.666
. However, research shows that

00:10:48.666 --> 00:10:50.300
even with a bad first experience

00:10:50.333 --> 00:10:52.600
, many people will chew it a second or third time.

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:53.900
Do you know why?

00:10:54.166 --> 00:10:55.333
Because the initial discomfort

00:10:55.333 --> 00:10:57.066
is actually due to the "medicinal effect."

00:10:57.066 --> 00:10:58.733
But quickly, your brain remembers

00:10:58.733 --> 00:11:00.700
the comfort and reward circuitry.

00:11:00.866 --> 00:11:02.133
After that, every time you eat it, your

00:11:02.133 --> 00:11:03.500
brain will immediately react,

00:11:03.500 --> 00:11:04.766
"Oh, something good is here

00:11:04.900 --> 00:11:07.100
!" At this point, it's difficult to quit.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.733
This feeling is similar to smoking

00:11:08.733 --> 00:11:10.600
, but betel nut has an additional problem:

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:12.300
it directly damages the oral cavity.

00:11:12.366 --> 00:11:14.333
Arecoline and the coarse fiber of the betel nut

00:11:14.333 --> 00:11:16.000
repeatedly rub against the oral mucosa.

00:11:16.133 --> 00:11:17.066
Over time,

00:11:17.100 --> 00:11:18.533
the mucosal cells are damaged,

00:11:18.533 --> 00:11:19.700
leading to fibrosis

00:11:19.733 --> 00:11:21.800
. After fibrosis, the mouth cannot open properly, and

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:22.600
the sense of taste declines.

00:11:22.600 --> 00:11:24.166
Continuing on, this leads to oral cancer.

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:26.933
In 1979, the incidence of oral cancer in Taiwan

00:11:26.933 --> 00:11:29.133
was only 3.4 cases per 100,000 people.

00:11:29.266 --> 00:11:30.400
By 2015,

00:11:30.400 --> 00:11:32.933
this number had surged to 22.8 cases.

00:11:33.000 --> 00:11:33.900
In more than 30 years,

00:11:33.900 --> 00:11:36.166
oral cancer has gone

00:11:36.166 --> 00:11:37.400
from a relatively marginal cancer

00:11:37.400 --> 00:11:39.566
to an inescapable shadow in the landscape of male cancers in Taiwan.

00:11:39.700 --> 00:11:41.166
According to data from the Ministry of Health and Welfare,

00:11:41.400 --> 00:11:44.666
in 2023,

00:11:44.666 --> 00:11:47.533
the number of new cases of oral, oropharyngeal, and hypopharyngeal cancer in Taiwan reached 8,522.

00:11:47.566 --> 00:11:50.700
Of these, 7,641 were male.

00:11:50.900 --> 00:11:52.166
These cancers aren't

00:11:52.166 --> 00:11:53.700
all caused by betel nut,

00:11:53.700 --> 00:11:55.133
but they all appear in

00:11:55.133 --> 00:11:56.566
the same everyday scenarios:

00:11:56.566 --> 00:11:59.366
truck cabs, construction site rest areas, fishing ports

00:11:59.366 --> 00:12:01.866
, night markets, and betel nut stands on mountain roads.

00:12:02.100 --> 00:12:03.300
These

00:12:03.300 --> 00:12:04.333
are the people who developed the disease;

00:12:04.333 --> 00:12:05.766
next are the people who died.

00:12:05.966 --> 00:12:08.966
In 2024, 3,687 people

00:12:08.966 --> 00:12:10.000
died of oral cancer in Taiwan

00:12:10.166 --> 00:12:11.733
, an average of 10 deaths per day

00:12:11.733 --> 00:12:14.066
. This number has not decreased significantly

00:12:14.100 --> 00:12:15.500
for five consecutive years.

00:12:15.733 --> 00:12:18.333
It ranks sixth among the top ten causes of cancer death in Taiwan.

00:12:18.333 --> 00:12:20.200
Of course, the vast majority are men,

00:12:20.366 --> 00:12:22.133
and young adults at that.

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:24.766
The number of male deaths was 3,372.

00:12:24.766 --> 00:12:25.933
If you calculate the proportion,

00:12:25.933 --> 00:12:26.966
out of a total of 3,600,

00:12:26.966 --> 00:12:28.366
3,300 were men.

00:12:28.600 --> 00:12:30.600
Many of them were at the age when their families faced

00:12:30.600 --> 00:12:32.666
the greatest financial pressure before developing the disease, working

00:12:32.766 --> 00:12:33.700
on construction sites during the day

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:35.000
and driving trucks for transport at night,

00:12:35.000 --> 00:12:35.966
or harvesting

00:12:35.966 --> 00:12:36.800
seafood in the mountains. While working,

00:12:36.800 --> 00:12:38.300
people would pop a betel nut into their mouths.

00:12:38.300 --> 00:12:39.200
At first, it would be a pick-me-up

00:12:39.266 --> 00:12:40.900
, but it gradually became a habit

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:41.466
, and then

00:12:41.466 --> 00:12:42.666
that was it.

00:12:42.800 --> 00:12:43.700
Most people

00:12:43.700 --> 00:12:45.000
wouldn't just eat betel nut; they

00:12:45.133 --> 00:12:46.300
would also smoke.

00:12:46.400 --> 00:12:47.400
A few years earlier, if they paired it with

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:49.333
steroidal liquors like styrax and bismuth subsalicylate,

00:12:49.333 --> 00:12:50.300
it would be the ultimate combination

00:12:50.300 --> 00:12:51.900
, completely ruining

00:12:51.900 --> 00:12:53.533
their health. This is

00:12:53.533 --> 00:12:54.900
the most complex and burdensome aspect

00:12:54.900 --> 00:12:56.300
of the betel nut business in Taiwan.

00:12:56.566 --> 00:12:58.533
It was once a high-yield crop on hillsides

00:12:58.533 --> 00:12:59.266
, benefiting farmers

00:12:59.266 --> 00:13:00.966
, providing business for vendors and vendors

00:13:00.966 --> 00:13:02.733
, and allowing laborers to earn a living.

00:13:02.733 --> 00:13:04.100
But it has also become

00:13:04.100 --> 00:13:06.600
one of the most difficult wounds to treat in Taiwan's public health system.

00:13:06.666 --> 00:13:08.500
According to the latest statistics from the National Health Insurance Administration,

00:13:08.566 --> 00:13:10.366
by 2025,

00:13:10.366 --> 00:13:12.700
the medical expenses for oral cancer in Taiwan will exceed NT$11.1 billion, and

00:13:13.100 --> 00:13:15.500
the medical expenses for esophageal cancer will exceed NT$4.1 billion.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:16.500
This means that Taiwan

00:13:16.533 --> 00:13:19.466
will spend NT$ 15.3 billion annually on the treatment of these two types

00:13:19.466 --> 00:13:21.700
of cancer, which are highly related to tobacco, alcohol, and betel nut

00:13:21.700 --> 00:13:23.333
consumption.

00:13:23.333 --> 00:13:25.400
Given the high cost

00:13:25.766 --> 00:13:27.600
of treatment , why

00:13:27.700 --> 00:13:29.333
hasn't Taiwan truly solved the betel nut problem

00:13:29.333 --> 00:13:31.466
over the decades

00:13:31.566 --> 00:13:32.433
? The reason is actually

00:13:32.433 --> 00:13:34.066
more complex than you might imagine.

00:13:35.600 --> 00:13:36.966
According to data from the Ministry of Agriculture,

00:13:37.066 --> 00:13:38.533
Taiwan's betel nut planting area

00:13:38.533 --> 00:13:40.933
in 2024 was 36,600 hectares,

00:13:41.100 --> 00:13:43.500
with a yield of 85.37 million kilograms.

00:13:43.533 --> 00:13:44.333
In the previous year

00:13:44.333 --> 00:13:47.000
, 2023, the area was 37,200 hectares,

00:13:47.133 --> 00:13:49.566
with a yield of 92.46 million kilograms.

00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:52.533
These figures indicate that the betel nut industry is declining

00:13:52.666 --> 00:13:54.266
, but not as quickly as you might think.

00:13:54.300 --> 00:13:56.533
Betel nut remains a huge agricultural business.

00:13:56.866 --> 00:13:58.900
Why is it so difficult for Taiwan's betel nut industry to decline

00:13:58.933 --> 00:14:00.733
? The primary reason is the farmers.

00:14:00.766 --> 00:14:02.366
It is a well-known fact that

00:14:02.466 --> 00:14:04.700
Taiwan's rural labor force is lacking and aging.

00:14:04.900 --> 00:14:06.500
Many betel nut plantation owners are already

00:14:06.500 --> 00:14:08.600
60-80 years old or older.

00:14:08.600 --> 00:14:09.566
For them,

00:14:09.666 --> 00:14:11.800
planting betel nut doesn't require much effort or physical strength

00:14:11.800 --> 00:14:12.666
. If you stop planting betel nut,

00:14:12.733 --> 00:14:14.266
those elderly farmers will ask you

00:14:14.266 --> 00:14:15.333
to cut down the trees. So

00:14:15.333 --> 00:14:16.366
what should I plant next?

00:14:16.566 --> 00:14:18.600
Let's set aside the old farmers for now.

00:14:18.600 --> 00:14:19.333
Some might say,

00:14:19.333 --> 00:14:20.400
"Then switch crops."

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:22.733
Actually, the government has considered solutions.

00:14:22.733 --> 00:14:24.066
As early as 2008,

00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:25.366
the agricultural authorities

00:14:25.366 --> 00:14:27.133
promoted the conversion of abandoned areca nut orchards to

00:14:27.300 --> 00:14:29.366
areca nut cultivation, with subsidies of NT$150,000 per hectare

00:14:29.666 --> 00:14:31.733
for field management fees, etc. These compensations and rewards

00:14:31.733 --> 00:14:33.166
sound quite generous.

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:35.566
But do you remember the figures we just mentioned?

00:14:35.700 --> 00:14:37.333
In 2024, Taiwan's areca nut planting

00:14:37.333 --> 00:14:39.466
area was still 36,600 hectares.

00:14:39.566 --> 00:14:41.200
The policy has been in place for nearly 20 years

00:14:41.200 --> 00:14:42.900
, and the area has only decreased from a peak of

00:14:42.900 --> 00:14:45.933
56,000 hectares to 36,600 hectares.

00:14:46.300 --> 00:14:47.900
In 20 years, only one-third has been reduced.

00:14:47.900 --> 00:14:48.733
What does this mean ? It

00:14:48.733 --> 00:14:51.333
means that this is not a problem that can be solved by subsidies.

00:14:51.466 --> 00:14:52.533
Farmers have to calculate

00:14:52.533 --> 00:14:54.100
much more complex issues than subsidies.

00:14:54.333 --> 00:14:55.533
Subsidies are a one-time issue

00:14:55.533 --> 00:14:57.566
; the risk of switching crops is long-term.

00:14:57.800 --> 00:14:58.900
The areca nut trees remain there,

00:14:58.900 --> 00:15:00.366
and although the price is lower year by year

00:15:00.366 --> 00:15:01.700
, there is still cash flow. After

00:15:01.766 --> 00:15:04.266
switching crops, farmers don't have stable income for the first few years.

00:15:04.266 --> 00:15:05.333
If they choose the wrong crop and

00:15:05.333 --> 00:15:06.133
the market collapses,

00:15:06.200 --> 00:15:07.966
they lose not only subsidies

00:15:07.966 --> 00:15:09.800
but also time, facility costs, and

00:15:09.800 --> 00:15:11.466
their last bit of confidence in farming.

00:15:11.600 --> 00:15:13.600
Another major problem with switching crops

00:15:13.800 --> 00:15:15.300
is that it's not something a single farmer

00:15:15.300 --> 00:15:16.466
can do alone.

00:15:16.466 --> 00:15:17.666
For example

00:15:17.666 --> 00:15:19.133
, if one person switches to papaya,

00:15:19.133 --> 00:15:20.533
they might still have distribution channels and sales

00:15:20.533 --> 00:15:22.333
, but if thousands of hectares in a township or county

00:15:22.366 --> 00:15:24.333
are planted simultaneously,

00:15:24.333 --> 00:15:27.300
the price of papaya in Taiwan will instantly collapse.

00:15:27.366 --> 00:15:28.166
Ultimately,

00:15:28.266 --> 00:15:30.966
there isn't a sufficiently stable industry to support the switch.

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:33.066
The second group squeezed out is the wholesalers.

00:15:33.266 --> 00:15:34.933
Outsiders only see

00:15:34.933 --> 00:15:36.700
roadside stalls and betel nut beauties;

00:15:36.766 --> 00:15:39.400
the real force behind distribution is the wholesalers in the producing areas.

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:41.200
Taiwanese betel nuts have long operated

00:15:41.200 --> 00:15:42.766
outside of regular wholesale markets ,

00:15:42.866 --> 00:15:44.133
with tiered pricing and distribution

00:15:44.133 --> 00:15:46.666
dominated by large local wholesalers

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:48.466
in Pingtung, Chiayi, and Nantou.

00:15:48.600 --> 00:15:50.133
Historically, wholesale prices

00:15:50.133 --> 00:15:52.400
have been controlled by major wholesalers in these three regions through a bidding mechanism.

00:15:52.500 --> 00:15:55.066
Chiayi's Zhongpu area is a core pricing hub across Taiwan.

00:15:55.400 --> 00:15:56.666
Goods from the production area

00:15:56.666 --> 00:15:58.100
are graded by wholesalers and priced

00:15:58.100 --> 00:15:59.133
according to size,

00:15:59.133 --> 00:16:00.066
with same-day shipments

00:16:00.066 --> 00:16:01.366
reaching stalls the next day for

00:16:01.366 --> 00:16:02.733
rapid capital recovery.

00:16:02.733 --> 00:16:04.033
This is a business reliant on experience

00:16:04.033 --> 00:16:05.533
and speed.

00:16:05.700 --> 00:16:06.933
The current situation is this:

00:16:06.933 --> 00:16:08.800
downstream stall owners are selling more slowly, and

00:16:08.800 --> 00:16:10.600
mid-tier wholesalers are becoming more conservative in

00:16:10.766 --> 00:16:12.166
their purchasing, which in turn forces wholesalers

00:16:12.166 --> 00:16:13.366
to be hesitant to buy in large quantities.

00:16:13.366 --> 00:16:14.200
Farmers, however

00:16:14.200 --> 00:16:16.000
, hope wholesalers will buy more,

00:16:16.000 --> 00:16:17.300
creating pressure on both ends.

00:16:17.300 --> 00:16:18.533
A single misjudgment

00:16:18.533 --> 00:16:21.100
could result in a backlog of unsold fresh fruit

00:16:21.100 --> 00:16:22.800
, which doesn't keep for long,

00:16:22.866 --> 00:16:24.500
making losses difficult to recover.

00:16:24.733 --> 00:16:26.033
Next comes

00:16:26.033 --> 00:16:27.900
the familiar betel nut stands and beauties

00:16:28.000 --> 00:16:30.766
– the most direct difficulties felt at the retail end.

00:16:30.766 --> 00:16:33.533
On one hand, Taiwan's health department's health promotions

00:16:33.533 --> 00:16:34.600
have reduced consumption

00:16:34.600 --> 00:16:35.966
, but a more important factor

00:16:35.966 --> 00:16:37.533
is the economic cycle.

00:16:37.800 --> 00:16:40.300
Taiwan's economy in 2000... Since the 2000s, growth has slowed,

00:16:40.366 --> 00:16:41.933
the blue-collar labor market

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:44.566
has shrunk, and the number of truck drivers and construction workers has decreased. With

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:46.666
fewer core consumers of betel nuts,

00:16:46.666 --> 00:16:48.000
the market naturally shrinks.

00:16:48.200 --> 00:16:49.966
After all, no matter how sexy a woman

00:16:49.966 --> 00:16:51.166
is or how scantily clad

00:16:51.166 --> 00:16:52.500
she is , she can't create

00:16:52.500 --> 00:16:53.466
demand for betel nuts

00:16:53.466 --> 00:16:55.533
out of thin air . Parking is also a major problem now

00:16:55.766 --> 00:16:57.000
, especially for large vehicles.

00:16:57.000 --> 00:16:58.900
Previously, it was possible to stop briefly on the roadside,

00:16:58.900 --> 00:17:00.466
but now traffic control is strict.

00:17:00.533 --> 00:17:01.766
For consumers,

00:17:01.766 --> 00:17:03.733
stopping on the way

00:17:03.733 --> 00:17:04.566
to quickly

00:17:04.566 --> 00:17:07.400
pick up the betel nut is a hassle; getting a traffic ticket for buying betel nuts is a real headache.

00:17:07.500 --> 00:17:10.166
Of course, it's not that there are no alternatives.

00:17:10.366 --> 00:17:12.733
Businesses in Chiayi have started using betel nuts to make slippers,

00:17:12.733 --> 00:17:14.866
supposedly because they have moisture-absorbing and antibacterial properties.

00:17:14.933 --> 00:17:16.533
Businesses in indigenous areas

00:17:16.533 --> 00:17:18.600
have also turned betel nuts into handicrafts

00:17:18.600 --> 00:17:20.200
, trying to explore the cultural and creative route.

00:17:20.300 --> 00:17:22.100
However, while these attempts are underway,

00:17:22.100 --> 00:17:24.533
the structural problems are ultimately unchangeable.

00:17:24.733 --> 00:17:26.700
Farmers are aging and worried about switching to other

00:17:26.766 --> 00:17:27.900
industries, wholesalers are worried

00:17:27.900 --> 00:17:30.566
about unsold inventory, stall owners are worried about parking tickets, and consumers are aging . Betel nut

00:17:30.600 --> 00:17:32.100
sellers are worried that if the industry disappears,

00:17:32.100 --> 00:17:33.333
they will have no other options.

00:17:33.333 --> 00:17:34.500
The retreat of an industry

00:17:34.500 --> 00:17:36.400
is never an abstract number.

00:17:36.466 --> 00:17:37.966
It represents individuals who

00:17:37.966 --> 00:17:39.500
don't know what to do tomorrow.

00:17:39.500 --> 00:17:40.733
You might ask,

00:17:40.733 --> 00:17:43.166
what is the government doing? In

00:17:43.400 --> 00:17:46.600
2024, a special law called the Areca Nut Act was drafted

00:17:46.666 --> 00:17:48.666
to systematically legislate on the planting

00:17:48.700 --> 00:17:51.000
, sales, health warnings, and

00:17:51.000 --> 00:17:53.533
transition protections for the areca nut industry.

00:17:53.700 --> 00:17:55.800
However, this law is still stuck.

00:17:55.866 --> 00:17:56.600
Why?

00:17:56.600 --> 00:17:57.966
Because if you restrict planting,

00:17:58.133 --> 00:17:59.133
farmers lose their "tickets"

00:17:59.133 --> 00:18:00.733
(a form of government funding); if you mandate health warnings,

00:18:00.766 --> 00:18:01.566
businesses refuse;

00:18:01.766 --> 00:18:02.966
if you compensate, transition

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:03.866
budgets are cut;

00:18:03.900 --> 00:18:05.100
the oral cancer mortality rate

00:18:05.100 --> 00:18:06.733
hasn't decreased for five consecutive years; and

00:18:06.733 --> 00:18:08.600
the bill hasn't passed for many years.

00:18:08.600 --> 00:18:10.400
This is

00:18:10.400 --> 00:18:11.600
the most realistic portrayal

00:18:11.666 --> 00:18:13.466
of the areca nut predicament in Taiwan . Everyone knows where the problem lies

00:18:13.466 --> 00:18:14.766
, but no one is willing to compromise.

00:18:15.000 --> 00:18:16.933
Finally, let's return to the initial question:

00:18:16.966 --> 00:18:19.500
what kind of business is the areca nut in Taiwan?

00:18:19.500 --> 00:18:21.066
Now you probably have the answer.

00:18:21.066 --> 00:18:23.200
It's rooted in the cultural soil of Taiwan's indigenous people.

00:18:23.200 --> 00:18:24.366
In 1,000,

00:18:24.366 --> 00:18:25.866
during the era of economic takeoff,

00:18:25.866 --> 00:18:27.666
betel nut became the most practical energy booster

00:18:27.666 --> 00:18:29.133
for countless blue-collar workers

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:31.333
. At the height of market competition,

00:18:31.333 --> 00:18:34.100
it gave rise to the unique betel nut beauty

00:18:34.166 --> 00:18:35.666
, transforming it into a spectacle

00:18:35.666 --> 00:18:36.500
, a symbol ,

00:18:36.500 --> 00:18:38.266
and a mirror of Taiwanese society.

00:18:38.266 --> 00:18:39.300
While the government neglected

00:18:39.300 --> 00:18:40.700
the pursuit of profit, it

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:41.533
experienced a period of rapid growth

00:18:41.566 --> 00:18:43.200
, culminating in the financial ruin of a family

00:18:43.200 --> 00:18:44.500
by a single cancer diagnosis.

00:18:44.700 --> 00:18:46.066
Betel nut itself had no inherent will;

00:18:46.366 --> 00:18:47.866
what truly turned it into what it is today

00:18:47.866 --> 00:18:48.766
is human desire,

00:18:48.766 --> 00:18:50.766
market profits, policy hesitation , and

00:18:50.933 --> 00:18:52.833
the lack of cheaper alternatives

00:18:52.833 --> 00:18:54.366
for an entire generation of blue-collar workers.

00:18:54.800 --> 00:18:55.633
The story of betel nut

00:18:55.633 --> 00:18:57.000
reflects Taiwanese society ; it records

00:18:57.066 --> 00:18:58.100
how that generation

00:18:58.100 --> 00:18:59.466
traded their bodies for a brick, a road

00:18:59.466 --> 00:19:00.700
, and an export ship—

00:19:00.700 --> 00:19:01.900
a contribution to

00:19:01.900 --> 00:19:03.366
Taiwan's economic miracle.

00:19:03.366 --> 00:19:05.066
That industry was in its twilight

00:19:05.166 --> 00:19:06.500
, its path still being explored

00:19:06.500 --> 00:19:07.800
, but the story of that generation

00:19:07.800 --> 00:19:09.766
may never be told again.

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:10.700
Thank you.

